    {
      "title": "Don't Skip This",
      "slug": "don-t-skip-this",
      "displayOrder": 5,
      "legacy": {
        "itemId": 873,
        "lessonOrder": 5
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<h3>It’s NOT “Just” a Blanket</h3>\r\n<h4><b>Swatching is NOT Optional</b></h4>\r\nWhen it comes to knitting the <span style=\"color: #9E2065; font-weight: bold;\">Seamless Color Block Blanket,</span> let me be clear: <span class=\"yellow_highlight\"> swatching is NOT optional.</span> <b>This isn’t a project where you can “guess” at gauge and hope for the best.</b><br>If your gauge is off, your blocks won’t be square, and the finished blanket won’t come together the way it should.\r\n<br><b>Thinking of using different yarns for the blocks?</b> That’s a fantastic way to get creative (and use up your stash), but here’s the deal: <span class=\"yellow_highlight\">you MUST swatch for each yarn.</span> Every yarn has its own characteristics, and without swatching, your “puzzle pieces” won’t fit together. \r\n\r\n<br>Planning to mix in different stitch patterns? Same rule applies—you MUST swatch in each stitch pattern to ensure consistency across the blocks.\r\n<br>This project is about more than just knitting a blanket. It’s about creating something you’ll be proud of, and that starts with preparation. <span class=\"yellow_highlight\">A little extra effort now will save you frustration later</span>—and you’ll end up with a beautiful, seamless blanket that’s everything you hoped for.\r\n\r\n\r\n <div class=\"videopopup\" data-videotitle=\"swatch2025\" data-vimeoid=\"1046394794\">\r\n\t\t<img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/1970153449-0dda23361c01cd76bf9e752ace4b3fa71355227555b08d98d3527000d94e47ec-d_1280x720?r=pad\">\r\n\t\t<div class=\"imagecenter text-center\"><button class=\"btn btn-sm\"><i class=\"fa fa-youtube-play fa-2x learn\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></button></div>\t\t\r\n</div><div class=\"text-center\"<br><h1> DON'T SKIP THIS!</h1></div>\r\n\r\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 10060,
              "order": 1
            }
          ],
          "title": "It&apos;s NOT \"just\" a blanket",
          "slug": "it-apos-s-not-just-a-blanket",
          "order": 1,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 6472,
            "blockType": "HTML"
          }
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "It's important that you recognize the construction of the stitches along the edge of your knitting.<br>Identify the loops that will be picked up with the Cut 'n Sew method.",
              "legacyComponentId": 10110,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "1051540009",
              "title": null,
              "legacyComponentId": 10099,
              "order": 2
            }
          ],
          "title": "Loops and Knots",
          "slug": "loops-and-knots",
          "order": 2,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 6486,
            "blockType": "HTML"
          }
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<span class=\"handwriting\" style=\"font-size:1.5em\">I HIGHLY SUGGEST trying this technique BEFORE starting your blanket.</span><br><ul class=\"lightlist\" style=\"list-style:none;\">\r\n<li>UNDERSTAND loops and knots and identify how to join</li>\r\n<li>Knit the EXACT same number of rows for each block</li>\r\n<li>Place markers at regular intervals for easier joining</li>\r\n<li>Don't mix 'n match gauges (or yarn with different gauges)</li>\r\n</ul>",
              "legacyComponentId": 10097,
              "order": 1
            },
